    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Emily added two 2-digit numbers correctly on paper. Then she painted out two cells, as shown. What is the sum of the two digits in the painted cells?",
    "image": "qimages/kangaroo/ca-2018-g0304/q07.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "5"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "7"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "8"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "9"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "13"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Work out the digits",
        "body": "The sum reads $\\square 2 + 3\\square = 57$.\n\n- Ones: $2 + \\square$ ends in 7. It can't be $2 + 15$, so the second hidden digit is 5 (and there is no carry).\n- Tens: $\\square + 3 = 5$, so the first hidden digit is 2.\n\nCheck: $22 + 35 = 57$ ✓. The two painted digits add up to $2 + 5 = 7$.\n\n**Answer: (B) 7**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Subtract",
        "body": "The painted digits make the numbers $a2$ and $3b$. Together $a2 + 3b = 57$ means $10a + b = 57 - 32 = 25$, so $a = 2$ and $b = 5$, and $a + b = 7$.\n\n**Answer: (B) 7**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "arithmetic",
      "logic"
    ],
    "difficulty": 1,
