      {
        "title": "List by the tens digit",
        "body": "The number has two different digits from 0, 1, 2, 5, 8 and lies between 12 and 58.\n\n- Tens digit 1: 15, 18 (10 and 12 are not greater than 12) → 2\n- Tens digit 2: 20, 21, 25, 28 → 4\n- Tens digit 5: 50, 51, 52 (58 is not smaller than 58) → 3\n- Tens digit 8: all are bigger than 58.\n\nTotal: $2 + 4 + 3 = 9$.\n\n**Answer: (E) 9**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Count all, then remove",
        "body": "Two-digit numbers with different digits from the set: the tens digit can be 1, 2, 5 or 8 (not 0) and the ones digit is any of the other 4 digits: $4 \\times 4 = 16$. Remove those not between 12 and 58: 10, 12 and 58, plus the four 80s (80, 81, 82, 85). $16 - 7 = 9$.\n\n**Answer: (E) 9**"
      }
    ],
