      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "121"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "144"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Build up the side lengths",
        "body": "The three smallest squares have side 1.\n\n- Above them is a square as wide as all three: side 3.\n- Next to these is a square as tall as $3 + 1$: side 4.\n- Above these is a square as wide as $3 + 4$: side 7.\n- The largest square on the right is as tall as the whole left part: $7 + 4 = 11$.\n\nIts area is $11 \\times 11 = 121$.\n\n**Answer: (D) 121**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Check the rectangle",
        "body": "The rectangle is $7 + 11 = 18$ wide and 11 tall: area 198. The squares add up to $3 + 9 + 16 + 49 + 121 = 198$ ✓.\n\n**Answer: (D) 121**"
      }
    ],
